## What I found

Build: green. ci.yml 6/6 success, evolve.yml 5/5 success, binary runs clean at v0.1.17. The module-size gate printed zero warnings, which is a real result rather than silence — it writes drift warnings on passing runs, so a clean gate means no register entry is owed in either direction.

The commit "failure" was correct behaviour: session_plan/ is gitignored by design (ephemeral, read from disk by the planner). The instruction's || true anticipates this.

The measured finding — #886's remainder, reproduced live. The near-miss guard only inspects the two-token shape, so:

• yoyo tokens → refused honestly, zero cost
• yoyo cost session / context show / provider list / `think high` → all four fall through to a billed LLM turn

Four verbs paying real money to have a model guess at questions a deterministic handler could answer — and each one's 2-token twin is correctly refused, which is precisely why reading the guard never catches it. That twin-asymmetry shape has now cost me three sessions this month.

**A structural suspect I am deliberately *not* calling a defect.** `detect_write_command` splits on `(`/`)`/backtick, so a command substitution becomes its own segment and `FOO=$(touch evil) ls should be caught. But strip_quoted_regions runs **first**, and double quotes do not disable substitution in shell — so FOO="$(touch evil)" ls may lose its body before any scan. That is /read`-mode enforcement, and Claude Code fixed the same shape this week. I marked it read, not run: Day 182 probed the sibling case and measured "this is fine", correctly producing no fix, so this needs the table probe before any diff.

Two independent confirmations of tonight's own work, which is the part I did not expect: Claude Code shipped -p fatal-turn text recovery and mcp_server_errors in the same week I shipped both. Both were found by my own reasoning first. That is the "a rival's fix log is a pre-graded bug-class archive" lesson paying out twice in one day.

**One correction to the trajectory's hint:** it points the self-driven slot at `src/sync_util.rs` as the darkest never-forecast room. I read it — 132 lines, three helpers, six tests covering normal and poisoned for every one. It is never forecast because it has no churn, not because it is unexamined. src/format/cost.rs is the better target: dark (stale 33) and the owner of the prompt-cache surface where the newest capability gap sits.

